## Defaults taken

- The nose picture is a close-up of one nose. The audit E19 offers a close-up or a child who
  points at the nose; the close-up reads better on a small card.
- The nose spec holds the id `l2-w01-check-row-nose` and the field `alsoIds`. The extra field
  `alsoDeliverAs` names the second delivered file, because one picture delivers two names.
- The specs of the props without an element sheet (the milk carton, the ten apples, the axe, the
  ostrich, the moon, the mango, the drum, and the two D4 prompts) hold an empty `references`
  list. The element sheets of the old pictures show the art that the audit rejects.
- The `use` of the nose spec is `check-row`. Both uses print at 360 px.
- The line art of a D4 prompt comes from its color picture, as the Muse path does for every
  picture. The D4 color picture is a black line drawing on white, so the line art twin stays a
  line drawing.
- The production batch files live in `docs/storytime/l2-unit1/judge/prod/`. The frozen kit in
  `docs/storytime/l2-unit1/judge/` is untouched.
- The batch script refuses to write over an existing batch file.

## Open question for the PM

The Workbooks picture list no longer holds the two D4 prompt ids. The delivery needs them before
the D4 pictures can ship. Workbooks maps the ids in its data when the art arrives, so no action
is needed now. The judge-set script still pins the list v5 SHA-256, so the kit cannot be rebuilt
against the current list. That is a separate decision for the closeout.

